course: dictionary
lesson: 3847
title: Foster: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Foster is a good example. «Foster carers look after children in their own homes when the children's parents can't.» Here foster means looking after a child for a time, in your own home.
explain: Foster can also mean looking after an animal for a time until it finds a new home. Animal shelters ask people to foster puppies and kittens. The clue is the animal: the puppy is cared for at home, but only until it has a new owner.
explain: Foster can also mean helping something grow or develop, as in «foster a love of reading». Nobody is living in a house here. Ask yourself what the word is attached to: a child, an animal, or an idea? The thing being fostered tells you the meaning.
fact: Foster is a verb: fosters, fostered, fostering.
fact: «Foster» means to look after a child for a time in your own home when the child's own family cannot care for them.
fact: «Foster» means to look after an animal for a time until it finds a new home.
fact: «Foster» means to help something grow or develop, as in «foster a love of reading».
fact: As an adjective, foster comes before a noun: «foster parent», «foster family», «foster child».
exercise: «Foster carers look after children in their own homes when the children's parents can't.» What does foster mean here? | To teach a child to swim at the pool | To take photos of a child on holiday | To buy a new bed for a child | *To look after a child for a time in your own home
exercise: Animal shelters ask people to foster puppies and kittens. What does foster mean here? | To take the puppies for a walk every day forever | To name the kittens after cartoon characters | To sell puppies and kittens in a shop | *To look after an animal for a time until it finds a new home
exercise: In school, a teacher wants to «foster a love of reading». What does foster mean? | *To help a love of reading grow | To cut pages out of books | To stop people reading in lessons | To count how many books the class has read
test: «Her foster mum, Jan, takes one look and fetches a proper suitcase with wheels.» What does foster mum mean? | *A mum who looks after a child for a time in her own home | A mum who sells suitcases | A mum who never leaves the house | A mum who works at a school
test: In «foster family», what kind of word is foster? | A verb, because it shows an action | A noun, because it names a thing | An adverb, because it tells you how the family acts | *An adjective, because it tells you what kind of family
exam: Which sentence uses foster to mean helping something grow? | Foster carers are checked and trained before they start | *Teachers foster good habits in their pupils | Animal shelters ask people to foster kittens | Her foster mum fetches a suitcase with wheels
